# NOTE on the ULTRAKILL material under apps/web/public, because the two kinds are
# not the same thing and were briefly treated as one.
#
# The gameplay capture (videos/ultrakill-powerup.mp4 and its poster) IS committed.
# It is a 33 second recording of a power-up the author wrote, running in the game:
# footage of his own mod, which is what every mod showcase publishes, and New Blood
# Interactive is explicitly mod-friendly. It is served in production on /parcours.
#
# The MESHES are not, and that is a different question. public/models/ultrakill/
# holds .glb files extracted from the shipped game, so publishing them would be
# redistributing New Blood's assets rather than showing the author's work. They
# are ignored by public/models/ultrakill/.gitignore and stay local; the page
# explains their absence to the reader instead of hiding it.

