programs/p01_stark_verifier/tests/c7_probe/Cargo.lock
apps/web/campaign-progress.jsonl

# 🚨 THE PROVER BUILD OUTPUT IS NOT THE PROVER WE SHIP, AND IT WAS COMMITTED.
#
# `wasm-pack` writes here. On 2026-08-22 this directory held — tracked in git —
# p01_stark_bg.wasm at 192,732 bytes (sha 4ace8913), the PRE-COSET build of
# 2026-05-06 that the DEPLOYED verifier rejects. The prover actually shipped is
# 267,610 bytes (sha 72a8c700) and lives in packages/stark-prover/wasm, which
# IS tracked on purpose. Both figures are pinned in
# packages/stark-prover/src/shippedBlob.test.ts: SHIPPED_BYTES = 267_610 /
# 72a8c700c466 is the circuit-7 build shipped now, and 229,640 / 51a947e3 is
# kept there as PRE_C7_BYTES, the pre-C7 coset build the tests refuse.
#
# The failure this caused before is measured and nasty: a rejected proof surfaces
# only at the END of a ~150-transaction buffer upload, never early. A directory
# named "wasm-out" is exactly where someone reaches for "the output".
#
# `stark/pkg/` was already ignored; this one was not. Kept on disk, out of git.
stark/wasm-out/

